  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "Dual-Mode Low-Rank Learner with Bridge-Prototype Ensemble for Vision-Language Class-Incremental Learning and HASTEN (Hierarchical Semantic Tree Anchoring) for Class-Incremental Learning in Visual-Textual Contexts",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Dual-Mode Low-Rank Learner (DuLBE) introduces a framework for class-incremental learning by combining dual-mode low-rank learning with a bridge-prototype ensemble classifier, enabling exemplar-free CIL while preserving visual and reasoning capabilities.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "HASTEN proposes a hierarchy-aware framework that uses semantic structure to stabilize CLIP-based CIL, reducing feature drift and catastrophic forgetting by leveraging external hierarchical knowledge.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both DuLBE and HASTEN demonstrate significant improvements in class-incremental learning across various benchmarks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
